      "obligation": "refuter:3:1",
      "id": "ex-completion-not-exact-without-finiteness",
      "location": "Verification, steps 2.1 and 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 2.1 proves only that the constructed x is not in im(\\widehat f). Step 3.1 then says: \"Therefore \\widehat f is not surjective, even though f sits in a short exact sequence. This is exactly the failure excluded by the finite-generation hypothesis.\" Non-surjectivity of the completion of f does not contradict exactness of the completed sequence, since f itself is not surjective. The proof must additionally show that x lies in the kernel of \\widehat M -> \\widehat{\\operatorname{coker}(f)}; that is true here but is not stated.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "7b529d30dad60d8510ed7009389503f69edec8d41ec270d1f61e0a092b5d775d"
    },
