      "location": "page prose, lines 22-25",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The page says that \"one iterated completion collapses to the same completed object because the two adic filtrations are cofinal.\" Its current dependency ex-iterated-adic-completions instead has the title \"Powers of an ideal give the same one-step adic completion\" and proves only \\widehat M^I \\cong \\widehat M^{I^r}, followed by the identity I+I^r=I (lines 25-50). A one-step cofinal-completion comparison does not establish an iterated-completion collapse.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "49b771d56ef814824e09b3bcab4cb797bf8bb9c90338f3091d5d12c1688ebf82"
