      "location": "library/commutative-algebra/inverse-limits-and-noetherian-completion-examples.md:22-25",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The B-page body says an iterated completion collapses because the adic filtrations are cofinal, but the current item `ex-iterated-adic-completions` proves only the one-step comparison `\\widehat M^I \\cong \\widehat M^{I^r} \\cong \\widehat M^{I+I^r}`. Reopening Stacks 10.96.2-10.96.3 shows that completion need not itself already be complete for arbitrary ideals, so cofinality alone does not justify the iterated-collapse sentence.",
